The upstream revision is licensed under Apache-2.0. The upstream checkout has no
NOTICE file at this revision (absent-at-frozen-revision); this NOTICE provides the repository attribution and
boundary record. The complete Apache text is reproduced in LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.

No upstream source tree, generated THREE.Group, fixture, model, texture, optional
integration, dependency lockfile, browser session, or runtime binary is bundled
under this directory. A fixed maintenance script can restore all tracked files
to an external isolation cache and verify the commit/tree/file hashes. The cache
is not product truth and must not be read or executed by the Runtime.

The first-party product adapter now admits only a bounded static ground-blade
ObjectSculptSpec projection into KnifeSceneProgram data; no upstream program is
executed. Callers provide only typed in-memory data; no caller path, URL, shell, TypeScript,
environment variable, secret, network access, SQLite/CAS write, or automatic
candidate confirmation is permitted. Upstream Python/Node/browser scripts remain
reference material until separately gated workers exist.

Optional upstream integrations are intentionally excluded from product adoption:
integrations/**, scripts/**, assets/**, skills/**, and all unreviewed forge Python
execution. Their package manifests and lockfiles are inventory evidence only.
